{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Cooling a hot part",
  "exampleId": "block-cooling",
  "description": "The part dissipates 10 W. It reaches the heatsink through 2 K/W, and the heatsink loses heat by convection (5 W/K, set by a signal) and by radiation. At steady state the heatsink sits 22.0 °C and the part 20 K hotter; the heat flow sensor reads the full 10 W. Below, a prescribed temperature holds one side of a 1 W/K conductor at 350 K while a prescribed heat flow adds 20 W from 1500 s, which lifts the body 20 K above it.",
  "duration": 3000,
  "revision": 0,
